    <string name="threshold_instruction">"\"L\" refers to brightness.Brightness increases as the value increases.

\"a\" refers to the value from green to red.

\"b\" refers to the value from blue to yellow.

L_min and L_max, a_min and a_max, b_min and b_max are the range of recognized values. 

If you want to recognize blue object, the steps are as follows:
1. Select blue in the box.
2. Adjust b_min to the minimum value 0, because blue \"b\" value is small in the Lab color model diagram.
3. Observe and adjust the white shape in the upper left frame to be the same as the blue sample, and other objects are in black.
4. Click \"Save\"."</string>
    <string name="threshold_instruction_1">L stands for brightness. The higher the value, the higher the brightness.</string>
    <string name="threshold_instruction_2">A is the component from green to red.</string>
    <string name="threshold_instruction_3">B is the component from blue to yellow.</string>
    <string name="threshold_instruction_4">Compared with RGB, CMYK and other color spaces, lab is more in line with human vision and easier to adjust: if you want to adjust the brightness, adjust the L channel; if you want to only adjust the color balance, adjust a and B respectively.</string>
